{**
 * c-tooltip - a short description of an element, shown while the pointer rests
 * on it or the focus is on it.
 *
 * The element is the caller's, written into the tooltipTarget block, and so is
 * the attribute that ties the two together: aria-describedby on the element,
 * naming $id. A tooltip describes; it is never all there is to name the
 * element, which has a name of its own - its text, or its aria-label when it is
 * drawn as an icon. tests/Template/TooltipTest asks both of every tooltip on
 * every page of the style guide.
 *
 * The tip is a manual popover, shown and hidden by assets/tooltip.ts rather than
 * by a click: on the pointer resting on the element and on the focus arriving
 * at it, kept while the pointer moves onto the tip itself or the focus stays,
 * and put away by Escape without the focus moving (WCAG 1.4.13). Manual also
 * means that showing it closes no menu it sits in. It is drawn in the top
 * layer, without a z-index.
 *
 * It hangs over the element, or under it when asked to, by CSS anchor
 * positioning, and turns to the other side when there is no room; a browser that
 * cannot anchor is served by assets/anchor.ts, which reads data-side.
 *
 * @param string $id the tip's id, which the element names in aria-describedby
 * @param string $side above or below: where the tip hangs when there is room
 *}

{define tooltip, string $id, string $text, string $side = 'above', ?string $testId = null}
    {* The holder is a flex box, so the whitespace between its children draws
       nothing and the markup can be laid out a part to a line. *}
    <span class="c-tooltip" style="anchor-name: --{$id}" data-testid="{$testId}">
        {block tooltipTarget}{/block}
        <span
            id="{$id}"
            class="c-tooltip__tip"
            role="tooltip"
            popover="manual"
            data-side="{$side === 'below' ? 'below' : 'above'}"
            style="position-anchor: --{$id}"
        >{$text}</span>
    </span>
{/define}
